---
title: Three surfaces of an agent-operable web UI
---
flowchart LR
  accTitle: Three surfaces of an agent-operable web UI
  accDescr: Shared UI behavior primitives emit three aligned surfaces in parallel—visual DOM and CSS for humans, ARIA and the accessibility tree for assistive technology, and a typed state and action index bridged to WebMCP document.modelContext for AI agents—avoiding fragile whole-DOM traversal.
  prim["Shared UI state + behaviors\n(e.g. @ui-sdk/core or app store)"]
  dom["Visual surface\nDOM + CSS layout"]
  a11y["Assistive surface\nARIA + accessibility tree"]
  idx["Agent surface\nsnapshot / query / act index"]
  gate["Safety boundary\nallow() gate + server authz"]
  webmcp["Browser tool bridge\nWebMCP document.modelContext"]
  scrape["Legacy fallback\nDOM / screenshot scraping"]

  prim --> dom
  prim --> a11y
  prim --> idx
  idx --> gate --> webmcp
  dom -. "brittle, high-token" .-> scrape

  class prim success
  class dom,a11y primary
  class idx,webmcp secondary
  class gate warning
  class scrape danger
